Moybyte's changes to Dropbear, all under DROPBEAR_MOY (port/localoptions.h) but
two splits that change no behaviour (session_loop's halves, svr_session_begin):
the server runs inside the kernel's process, one session served at a time.

- sysoptions.h: the tracking allocator is on, so a session's allocations
  are freed with its epoch when it ends (moy_ssh.c).
- dbmalloc.c: the allocator's calloc/realloc/free are DB_CALLOC/DB_REALLOC/
  DB_FREE, PSRAM and counted on a board (port/moy_ssh_port.h).
- svr-session.c and session.h: an exit jumps back to the accept loop
  instead of exit(); the log is moy_ssh_log; no unauthenticated close delay
  (one task). svr_session_begin is a session set up without its loop, which
  the second connection's runs in turns.
- common-session.c: no signal pipe; the command's end is polled every loop.
  The loop's halves are session_loop_fds and session_loop_step, and between
  them it gives moy_ssh.c its turn (moy_ssh_loop_fds, moy_ssh_loop_heard):
  the listening socket, and a second connection's session signing in beside
  the one served (moy_ssh.c, THE TAKEOVER).
- common-channel.c and channel.h: moy_channels_end, every channel told why
  and closed, for the session a newer sign-in ends; moy_channel_refuse, a
  channel told why on its stderr and left to close, for a refused command.
- svr-chansession.c: no fork, no pty, no SIGCHLD: a session's command is
  moy_ssh_command (the shell's face over a socket pair), its end
  moy_ssh_reap, its signal moy_ssh_signal; a pty request keeps the size.
  A command's end does not flush its output: the output ends at the face's
  close, which follows its status, so the bytes still crossing the board's
  loopback when the status is reaped are read, not dropped. A command
  moy_ssh_command refuses with a reason (the face another transport holds)
  is a request taken: the reason on the client's stderr, its status 1, and
  the channel's close, where a channel failure would tell the client
  nothing.
- chansession.h: the size a pty request asked for.
- dbrandom.c: the seed is the SoC's hardware generator (moy_ssh_entropy).
- gensignkey.c: the host key is renamed into place (FAT has no link()).
- svr-kex.c: the made-key log's fingerprint only where the build has it
  (DROPBEAR_SIGNKEY_VERIFY): a server without public-key sign-in does not.
- libtomcrypt's crypt_cipher_descriptor.c and crypt_hash_descriptor.c: the
  tables are PSRAM, taken at setup (port/moy_ssh_port.h), not .bss.
- common-algo.c and algo.h: the algorithm lists, which a session writes
  (`usable`), are const tables copied at setup into PSRAM (moy_ssh_algos),
  each list's name a pointer to its copy, not .data.
- svr-authpubkey.c: the authorized keys are the store's, read by the server
  at the connection's start (moy_ssh_keys), not a file under a home folder.

